<!--
  The third-party code fw-app.jar carries and where its license terms and notices travel with it (M10 binary notices).
  Each upstream jar's own LICENSE, NOTICE and DEPENDENCIES files are copied unchanged into META-INF/licenses/ARTIFACT/
  (handoff/outbox/devtools/notices/extract_notices.sh), and the shade step drops the colliding originals, so no jar's
  file silently replaces another's. "packages" are the class and resource roots each component owns in the jar; the
  packaged-jar test requires every third-party entry of the jar to fall under one of them. The project's own terms are
  the author's LICENSE and NOTICE.md (LicenseRef-BUSL-1.1, named in every source header).
-->
